 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT relating to payments in lieu of taxes paid to the Minisink Valley\ncentral school district",
    "basePrintNo": "S5769",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5769-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Education",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S5769\n\nSPONSOR: METZGER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act relating to payments in lieu of taxes paid to\nthe Minisink Valley central school district\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nRelates to payments in lieu of taxes (PILOT) paid to the Minisink Valley\nCentral School District\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of the bill will make changes to the real property tax cap\nquantity change factor for the the Minisink Valley Central School\nDistrict on the PILOT paid to by Competitive Power Ventures to provide\nthat the change in assessed value for each property on the exempt side\nof the tax roll for this PILOT agreement.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe current Real Property Tax Cap law does not account for improvements\nmade on a property when a PILOT is cited there, nor does it address the\nfiscal issues regarding the expected tax payments on the balance sheet\nthat would have been due to a school district, but no longer will be\npaid due to the PILOT coming online. Under current law, when the PILOT\nis new, the Tax Base Growth Factor does not count these real property\ntax improvements which causes an inequity in the calculation.\n\nThis bill will address the accounting of a specific PILOT payment within\nthe tax cap calculation for the Minisink School District for the new\nPILOT from Competitive Power Ventures (CPV). The impact of this PILOT on\nthe allowable growth of the tax levy for the Minisink school community\ncreates a serious school budget issue and a negative tax cap for the\nschool district budget that must be addressed.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the state\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
